From 30ccea79522739cb08ec19ceb2fc35bbc86fa3b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:34:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: write log lines on a logger thread

Move enabled line rendering and sink I/O off producer threads into per-thread
bounded rings and a logger consumer. Prepare rings at thread startup and
reuse exited rings. Final capacity is131072 records of512bytes (64MiB of
reserved slot storage per prepared thread, metadata extra); lazy raw storage
does not imply that all reserved pages are initially resident.

Debug/info overflow is dropped and counted. Warnings/errors use consumer
backpressure; errors wait for a consumer pass and flushed sinks. Consumer
callbacks use a reserved severe-overflow record without recursive callbacks.
Wake publication avoids a producer mutex. Preserve live-consumer shutdown,
atexit drain, pause quiescence, reopen/path ordering and explicit Flush.
Flush older records before existing logging-RPC capture/category boundaries;
start functional helper deadlines after the context action. Retain causal
regressions for the repaired boundaries and consumer behavior.

Historical flood caller timing excluded many dropped records and is not a
sink-throughput result. The final interleaved stock/new/Quill/NanoLog matrix
is outstanding. This composition is not a new benchmark or platform claim.

